From: SG Quality Lead R8 <danswett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:10:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] CI S2: prime-playwright-cache.yml fills the apt archives
 cache FULL restores, automatically, on main only, saving the exact key only
 after every deb verified (Part of #4104)

Prime-cache, its own workflow patch for Quality. Patch branch: sg-patch/ci-s2-prime-cache-4104.
BASE: apply on ci/s2-combined3 at its head 58e2a977dd06d2574d9d929d14c11d3e1b893bc7 (#4503 with Q10's merge of main and the stale-PWA text fix), or on main once #4503 has merged.

AUTOMATIC: a push to main that changes the system-packages action, this workflow or a package lock (paths-filtered), a DAILY schedule, and workflow_dispatch. NO pull_request, pull_request_target or
workflow_run. Permissions: contents: read only (actions: write is NOT needed: actions/cache saves through the runner's cache service; only the REST delete API needs it). The job runs only on refs/heads/main, so a
dispatch from a branch runs nothing: the README says to dispatch on main. Concurrency: one group, cancel-in-progress false. The save key is exactly the restore key (cache-key is steps.debs.outputs.cache-primary-key);
the save step is the step right after the download, runs on success() and cache-ready, and download.sh says cache-ready only after the last check of every .deb against the signed index, so a download that did
not verify is never saved. action.yml's text (lines 8 and 27) now says prime-playwright-cache.yml saves, not ci.yml. Pinned by PrimeCacheWorkflowTests (red first; mutations caught).

